I have gathered a complete picture. Here is my thorough report.

## Summary

The repository is a PetClinic (OfficeFloor + Spring) app. Owner duplicate/identity detection lives under `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`. Notably, there is a discrepancy between what the acceptance test describes (an "identity-key-v2" using SHA-256 + soundex, 64-hex) and the actual implementation (a plaintext pipe-joined key; soundex is not implemented anywhere). Details below.

---

## 1. identityKey computation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerIdentity.java` — the single source of the identity key. It is NOT a SHA-256 hash; it is a plaintext pipe-joined string of `telephone | email | householdId`:
```java
20  public static String key(Owner owner) {
21      return segment(owner.getTelephone()) + '|' + segment(owner.getEmail()) + '|'
22              + segment(owner.getHouseholdId());
23  }
25  private static String segment(String value) {
26      return value == null || value.isBlank() ? "" : value;
27  }
```

Exposed on the DTO via MapStruct in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:
```java
48  @Mapping(target = "identityKey",
49      expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.OwnerIdentity.key(owner))")
```
Documented in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2207-2216 (example `'+61412345678||3f2a1b0c9d8e'`, plaintext, NOT 64-hex).

Note: `identityKey` is a derived DTO-only field — there is no `identityKey` column in the `Owner` entity (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` has `householdId`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `namesakeCount` columns only).

## 2. Duplicate detection returning HTTP 409

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` — the hard-block. Compares whole identity keys across non-deleted owners; throws `DuplicateIdentityException` when a match exists, unless `sharesHousehold` is set:
```java
21  public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val Boolean sharesHousehold, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
22          throws DuplicateIdentityException {
23      if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(sharesHousehold)) {
24          return; // declared household member: allowed to join an existing household
25      }
26      String identityKey = OwnerIdentity.key(owner);
27      boolean inUse = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
28              .filter(existing -> !existing.getId().equals(owner.getId()))
29              .filter(existing -> !Boolean.TRUE.equals(existing.getDeleted())) // ignore soft-deleted owners
30              .anyMatch(existing -> identityKey.equals(OwnerIdentity.key(existing)));
31      if (inUse) {
32          throw new DuplicateIdentityException(
33                  "An owner with identity key " + identityKey + " already exists");
34      }
35  }
```

The 409 response chain:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java` (checked exception).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java` — responds `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` with a ProblemDetail (`errors: ["identityKey"]`):
```java
13  ProblemDetail detail = ProblemDetails.build(ex, HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
14          "An owner with the same identityKey already exists");
15  detail.setProperty("errors", java.util.List.of("identityKey"));
16  response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CONFLICT).body(detail));
```
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml` wires the handler.

## 3. householdId computation and household-duplicate block

